 "face": {
  "mode": "baked",
  "note": "The face is baked on the ball: the eyes are glossy lenses (lo_eyes) with the blue iris, the pupil and two catchlights painted in; the small open smile (navy, a lighter tongue, two tiny fangs) and the closed lids' lash lines are baked into the body. No face sheet and no morphs: expressions in clips' `faces` are hints only; the mouth never opens. Blinking scales the blink bones (play `blink` over any clip): each lens squashes onto the painted lash line and sinks under the skin. The glow is the ORM alpha in each texel's own colour: a low floor on the cyan, the white core round the mouth and the back star hot, the wings' and the tail's rims and the sparks bright; socket_core is the ball's centre.",
